WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.472
ROW_NUMBER, RANK, and DENSE_RANK look similar until ties occur.

00:00:04.472 --> 00:00:07.692
ROW_NUMBER always assigns a unique sequence.

00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:12.092
RANK gives equal values the same rank and leaves gaps afterward.

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:16.062
DENSE_RANK also shares ranks but does not leave gaps.

00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:20.377
Choose the function based on what ties should mean for the business question.

00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:24.127
Ranking functions differ mainly in how they handle ties.

00:00:24.127 --> 00:00:31.282
ROW_NUMBER forces a unique sequence, RANK leaves gaps after ties, and DENSE_RANK does not.

00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:35.307
Add deterministic tie-breakers when a unique order matters;

00:00:35.307 --> 00:00:39.516
otherwise two executions can choose different rows among tied values.
